> API and interpretation

The compatibility result clears its order on cycles; run output separately
retains actual emitted vertices, remaining indegrees and n-sentinel positions
for unprocessed vertices. Level values are exact longest-path levels only for
DAGs; on blocked vertices they are the lower bounds actually propagated from
emitted sources. The independent order checker validates a complete permutation
and every edge without rerunning Kahn.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Kahn, Topological Sorting of Large Networks, CACM5 (1962),558-562|https://doi.org/10.1145/368996.369025]

